    "expectedRule": "Chapter 8 has two anchors that both start uncalibrated: the first clear of past_calibration_anchor sets pastCalibrated, the first clear of future_calibration_anchor sets futureCalibrated. Display: title 时间校准, status `0/2 时序漂移` (danger), `1/2 单锚锁定` (warning) or `2/2 双锚同步` (resolved, targetReached), meter {calibrated, 2}. While the past anchor is uncalibrated encounters get +20% defense; while the future anchor is uncalibrated traps get +20% damage and DC (rounded up); the boss bonus applies only in the boss encounter. With mist_breathing as the main method every trap is seen through, so a risked trap deals max(4, floor(damage x 0.45)): aged_gear_trap 62 drifting -> ceil(74.4) = 75 -> 33; zero_meridian 64 calibrated -> 28. Run pressure stays 0% below 6 clears. Gates: temporal_past_shortcut (past_shortcut_foyer -> erased_patrol) needs the past anchor and reads `先校准过去锚点后开放。`; temporal_future_shortcut (future_shortcut_foyer -> accelerated_patrol) needs the future anchor and reads `先校准未来锚点后开放。`; temporal_calibration_bridge (calibration_bridge -> zero_hour_regent) needs both and reads `过去与未来锚点均校准后开放。`; a closed gate is not a legal destination. The epoch sentinels are elites, so their loot offer is declined (node/resolve-equipment-loot without an item) before moving on. The pursuer is a separate run system and is disabled after entry so it cannot ambush the walk. All expected values are frozen here, never read from candidate code."
  },
